12413: Type            SCK2      RESET         CPU          each section
12414: Power-on reset                          Initialized
12415: Manual reset    High      Low           Initialized
12416: 
12417:                 Low       Low
12418: 
12419: (3) H-UDI Reset
12420: 
12421: � Source: SDIR.TI3-TI0 = B'0110 (negation) or B'0111 (assertion)
12422: � Transition address: H'A000 0000
12423: � Transition operations:
12424: 
12425:     Exception code H'000 is set in EXPEVT, initialization of VBR and SR is performed, and a
12426:     branch is made to PC = H'A000 0000.
12427:     In the initialization processing, the VBR register is set to H'0000 0000, and in SR, the MD,
12428:     RB, and BL bits are set to 1, the FD bit is cleared to 0, and the interrupt mask bits (IMASK)
12429:     are set to B'1111.
12430:     CPU and on-chip peripheral module initialization is performed. For details, see the register
12431:     descriptions in the relevant sections.
12432: 
12433:    H-UDI_reset()
12434:    {
12435: 
12436:          EXPEVT = H'00000000;
12437:          VBR = H'00000000;
12438:          SR.MD = 1;
12439:          SR.RB = 1;
12440:          SR.BL = 1;
12441:          SR.IMASK = B'1111;
12442:          SR.FD = 0;
12443:          Initialize_CPU();
12444:          Initialize_Module(PowerOn);
12445:          PC = H'A0000000;
12446:    }
12447: 
12448:                                         Rev.7.00 Oct. 10, 2008 Page 161 of 1074
12449:                                                                        REJ09B0366-0700
12450: Section 5 Exceptions
12451: 
12452: (4) Instruction TLB Multiple-Hit Exception
12453: 
12454: � Source: Multiple ITLB address matches
12455: � Transition address: H'A000 0000
12456: � Transition operations:
12457: 
12458:     The virtual address (32 bits) at which this exception occurred is set in TEA, and the
12459:     corresponding virtual page number (22 bits) is set in PTEH [31:10]. ASID in PTEH indicates
12460:     the ASID when this exception occurred.
12461:     Exception code H'140 is set in EXPEVT, initialization of VBR and SR is performed, and a
12462:     branch is made to PC = H'A000 0000.
12463:     In the initialization processing, the VBR register is set to H'0000 0000, and in SR, the MD,
12464:     RB, and BL bits are set to 1, the FD bit is cleared to 0, and the interrupt mask bits (IMASK)
12465:     are set to B'1111.
12466:     CPU and on-chip peripheral module initialization is performed in the same way as in a manual
12467:     reset. For details, see the register descriptions in the relevant sections.
12468: 
12469:    TLB_multi_hit()
12470:    {
12471: 
12472:          TEA = EXCEPTION_ADDRESS;
12473:          PTEH.VPN = PAGE_NUMBER;
12474:          EXPEVT = H'00000140;
12475:          VBR = H'00000000;
12476:          SR.MD = 1;
12477:          SR.RB = 1;
12478:          SR.BL = 1;
12479:          SR.IMASK = B'1111;
12480:          SR.FD = 0;
12481:          Initialize_CPU();
12482:          Initialize_Module(Manual);
12483:          PC = H'A0000000;
12484:    }
12485: 
