The archived source confirms both EXPEVT defects. I also found two problems in the brief: an interrupt’s temporary rewrite would be discarded before EXPEVT is stored, and both proposed row names are too long for the gate’s two-space matcher. I’m checking the remaining coverage claims and the manual’s user-break behavior.
