12490: (5) Operand TLB Multiple-Hit Exception
12491: 
12492: � Source: Multiple UTLB address matches
12493: � Transition address: H'A000 0000
12494: � Transition operations:
12495: 
12496:     The virtual address (32 bits) at which this exception occurred is set in TEA, and the
12497:     corresponding virtual page number (22 bits) is set in PTEH [31:10]. ASID in PTEH indicates
12498:     the ASID when this exception occurred.
12499:     Exception code H'140 is set in EXPEVT, initialization of VBR and SR is performed, and a
12500:     branch is made to PC = H'A000 0000.
12501:     In the initialization processing, the VBR register is set to H'0000 0000, and in SR, the MD,
12502:     RB, and BL bits are set to 1, the FD bit is cleared to 0, and the interrupt mask bits (IMASK)
12503:     are set to B'1111.
12504:     CPU and on-chip peripheral module initialization is performed in the same way as in a manual
12505:     reset. For details, see the register descriptions in the relevant sections.
12506: 
12507:    TLB_multi_hit()
12508:    {
12509: 
12510:          TEA = EXCEPTION_ADDRESS;
12511:          PTEH.VPN = PAGE_NUMBER;
12512:          EXPEVT = H'00000140;
12513:          VBR = H'00000000;
12514:          SR.MD = 1;
12515:          SR.RB = 1;
12516:          SR.BL = 1;
12517:          SR.IMASK = B'1111;
12518:          SR.FD = 0;
12519:          Initialize_CPU();
12520:          Initialize_Module(Manual);
12521:          PC = H'A0000000;
12522:    }
