12526: Section 5 Exceptions
12527: 
12528: 5.6.2 General Exceptions
13150:     execution type exception, the branch instruction PR register write operation (PC  PR
13151:     operation performed in BSR, BSRF, JSR) is inhibited.
13152: 
13153: 5.7 Usage Notes
13154: 
13155: 1. Return from exception handling
13156:     a. Check the BL bit in SR with software. If SPC and SSR have been saved to external
13157:         memory, set the BL bit in SR to 1 before restoring them.
13158:     b. Issue an RTE instruction. When RTE is executed, the SPC contents are set in PC, the SSR
13159:         contents are set in SR, and branch is made to the SPC address to return from the exception
13160:         handling routine.
13161: 
13162: 2. If a general exception or interrupt occurs when SR.BL = 1
13163:     a. General exception
13164:         When a general exception other than a user break occurs, a manual reset is executed. The
13165:         value in EXPEVT at this time is H'0000 0020; the value of the SPC and SSR registers is
13166:         undefined.
13167:     b. Interrupt
13168:         If an ordinary interrupt occurs, the interrupt request is held pending and is accepted after
13169:         the BL bit in SR has been cleared to 0 by software. If a nonmaskable interrupt (NMI)
13170:         occurs, it can be held pending or accepted according to the setting made by software. In the
13171:         sleep or standby state, however, an interrupt is accepted even if the BL bit in SR is set to 1.
13172: 
13173: 3. SPC when an exception occurs
13174:     a. Re-execution type general exception
13175:         The PC value for the instruction in which the general exception occurred is set in SPC, and
13176:         the instruction is re-executed after returning from exception handling. If an exception
13177:         occurs in a delay slot instruction, however, the PC value for the delay slot instruction is
13178:         saved in SPC regardless of whether or not the preceding delayed branch instruction
13179:         condition is satisfied.
13180:     b. Completion type general exception or interrupt
13181:         The PC value for the instruction following that in which the general exception occurred is
13182:         set in SPC. If an exception occurs in a branch instruction with delay slot, however, the PC
13183:         value for the branch destination is saved in SPC.
