10127: 
10128: 1. UTLB address array read
10129:     VPN, D, V, and ASID are read into the data field from the UTLB entry corresponding to the
10130:     entry set in the address field. In a read, associative operation is not performed regardless of
10131:     whether the association bit specified in the address field is 1 or 0.
10132: 
10133: 2. UTLB address array write (non-associative)
10134:     VPN, D, V, and ASID specified in the data field are written to the UTLB entry corresponding
10135:     to the entry set in the address field. The A bit in the address field should be cleared to 0.
10136: 
10137: 3. UTLB address array write (associative)
10138:     When a write is performed with the A bit in the address field set to 1, comparison of all the
10139:     UTLB entries is carried out using the VPN specified in the data field and PTEH.ASID. The
10140:     usual address comparison rules are followed, but if a UTLB miss occurs, the result is no
10141:     operation, and an exception is not generated. If the comparison identifies a UTLB entry
10142:     corresponding to the VPN specified in the data field, D and V specified in the data field are
10143:     written to that entry. If there is more than one matching entry, a data TLB multiple hit
10144:     exception results. This associative operation is simultaneously carried out on the ITLB, and if a
10145:     matching entry is found in the ITLB, V is written to that entry. Even if the UTLB comparison
10146:     results in no operation, a write to the ITLB side only is performed as long as there is an ITLB
10147:     match. If there is a match in both the UTLB and ITLB, the UTLB information is also written to
10148:     the ITLB.
10149: 
10150: Rev.7.00 Oct. 10, 2008 Page 106 of 1074
10151: REJ09B0366-0700

